ManSection.Description:
    Default values for start and finish are 1 and the limit
    imposed by the Small Groups Library, respectively.
    If the option nonsolvable is set, solvable groups are omitted.


gap> iter := SmallGroupsIterator();
<iterator running over the Small Groups Library>
gap> First(iter,G->not IsAbelian(G));
<pc group of size 6 with 2 generators>
gap> StructureDescription(last);
"S3"
gap> First(iter,G->not IsAbelian(G) and IsSimple(G));
Alt( [ 1 .. 5 ] )
gap> ForAny(SmallGroupsIterator(1,59),
>           G->not IsAbelian(G) and IsSimple(G));
false
gap> ForAny(SmallGroupsIterator(1,60),
>           G->not IsAbelian(G) and IsSimple(G));
true
gap> ForAll(SmallGroupsIterator(61,119),G->IsSolvable(G));
true
gap> iter := SmallGroupsIterator();
<iterator running over the Small Groups Library>
gap> G := First(iter,G->CommutatorLength(G)<>1);
<pc group of size 96 with 6 generators>
gap> StructureDescription(G);
"((C4 x C2) : C4) : C3"

    Default values for start and finish are 1 and the degree
    limit imposed by the Transitive Groups Library, respectively.


gap> iter := TransitiveGroupsIterator(); 
<iterator running over the Transitive Groups Library>
gap> NextIterator(iter);
S2
gap> NextIterator(iter);
A3
gap> NextIterator(iter);
S3
gap> NextIterator(iter);
C(4) = 4
gap> NextIterator(iter);
E(4) = 2[x]2
gap> NextIterator(iter);
D(4)
gap> NextIterator(iter);
A4
gap> NextIterator(iter);
S4
gap> iter := TransitiveGroupsIterator();
<iterator running over the Transitive Groups Library>
gap> First( iter, G -> not IsSolvable(G) and IsPrimitive(G)
>                      and Transitivity(G,MovedPoints(G)) < 2 );
A_5(10)
gap> L := [];;
gap> for G in TransitiveGroupsIterator(4,6) do Add(L,G); od;
gap> L;
[ C(4) = 4, E(4) = 2[x]2, D(4), A4, S4, C(5) = 5, D(5) = 5:2, 
  F(5) = 5:4, A5, S5, C(6) = 6 = 3[x]2, D_6(6) = [3]2, D(6) = S(3)[x]2, 
  A_4(6) = [2^2]3, F_18(6) = [3^2]2 = 3 wr 2, 2A_4(6) = [2^3]3 = 2 wr 3, 
  S_4(6d) = [2^2]S(3), S_4(6c) = 1/2[2^3]S(3), F_18(6):2 = [1/2.S(3)^2]2,
  F_36(6) = 1/2[S(3)^2]2, 2S_4(6) = [2^3]S(3) = 2 wr S(3), 
  L(6) = PSL(2,5) = A_5(6), F_36(6):2 = [S(3)^2]2 = S(3) wr 2, 
  L(6):2 = PGL(2,5) = S_5(6), A6, S6 ]

    Default values for start and finish are 1 and the limit
    imposed by the Perfect Groups Library, respectively.


gap> iter := PerfectGroupsIterator();
<iterator running over the Perfect Groups Library>
gap> NextIterator(iter);
Idgroup
gap> NextIterator(iter);
A5
gap> NextIterator(iter);
A5 2^1
gap> NextIterator(iter);
L3(2)
gap> iter := PerfectGroupsIterator();;
gap> First(iter,G->Size(Centre(G)) > RootInt(Size(G),3));
A5 2^1 x ( 2^4 E ( 2^1 A x 2^1 A ) ) C ( 2^1 x 2^1 )
gap> Size(Centre(G));
32
gap> Size(G);
30720
gap> 32^3;
32768
gap> iter := PerfectGroupsIterator(100000);
<iterator running over the Perfect Groups Library>
gap> NextIterator(iter);
A5 2^1 29^2
gap> 
gap> NextIterator(iter);
L2(59)
gap> NextIterator(iter);
